anizers say, using last year's winner as the example.\\n\\n\\\"In the week following the 2017 winner announcement,\\\" the foundation reports, \\\"sales of ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2018/07/man-booker-prize-fiction-longlist-2018-announced-london/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d15\"},\"ref\":\"d15\",\"snippet\":\" ... time to any work published in the United Kingdom and written in (not translated into) the English language.\\n\\nThere have been three special awards celebrating the Booker's history. In 1993, the \\\"Booker of Bookers\\\" prize was awarded to Salman Rushdie for Midnight's Children (the 1981 winner ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d53\"},\"ref\":\"d53\",\"snippet\":\" ... These three women and their families, their losses and loves, unwind against a backdrop of a rapidly changing Oman. Winner of the 2019 Man Booker International Prize.\\n\\nRequest Book | Request E-Book | Request Audiobook\\n\\nAccessible editions: BK\\n\\nSet in Iran in the decade following the 1979 Revolution, this ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.nypl.org/spotlight/world-literature-festival/recommended-translations\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"062e7189ba80a20593709d1caec2c038fd388aaf709717e6a2c373b241aeae60\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"e34aab8298fe341b1ec208764cb4da17c4360bf06724015779489e5eb5a4e6ea\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Man Booker International Prize 2017 winner Love in the Time of Cholera\",\"view\":\"full\