rs/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d15\"},\"ref\":\"d15\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2010 The Booker Prizes |url= |access-date=2022-10-19 |website=thebookerprizes.com |language=en |archive-date=6 February 2023 |archive-url= |url-status=live }} | Shortlist | Damon Galgut | In a Strange Room | Atlantic Books | *Andrew Motion (chair) *Rosie Blau *Deborah Bull *Tom Sutcliffe *Frances Wilson |\\n| 2010 The Booker ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d21\"},\"ref\":\"d21\",\"snippet\":\" ... His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"98d75c7844a460c41bf286a87f8bff79c8ced52517c67cf04fbf84aff268f8b2\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"7c88a6b6518f2edfe2b441620e547ebca1f9d14ece354e834d665d9672ec3724\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"book translated 25 languages shortlisted International Booker Prize 2010s\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d9\"},\"ref\":\"d9\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 2018, the Polish novelist was recognized for \\\"Flights,\\\" which she calls a \\\"constellation novel,\\\" owing to its fragmentary form and genre-defying style, and which won that year's Man Booker Prize. \\\"Drive Your Plow Over the Bones of the Dead,\\\" her latest novel to be translated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.newyorker.com/books/page-turner/the-2019-national-book-awards-longlist-translated-literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d14\"},\"ref\":\"d14\",\"snippet\":\" ... Unlike the Booker Prize, short story collections are eligible for the International Booker Prize. The £50,000 prize money is split evenly between the author and translator of the winning novel.\\n\\nHistory and administration\\n\\nThe prize was established as the \\\"Booker Prize for Fiction\\\" after the company Booker ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d19\"},\"ref\":\"d19\",\"snippet\":\" ... In London, Geetanjali Shree and Daisy Rockwell Win the 2022 International Booker Prize\\nauthor: Porter Anderson\\ndate: 2022-05-26\\n---\\n'Tomb of Sand' is the first novel translated from an Indian language to win the award. Shree and Rockwell split the International Booker's £50,000 purse.\\n\\nBy ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2022/05/geetanjali-shree-and-daisy-rockwell-win-the-international-booker-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d11\"},\"ref\":\"d11\",\"snippet\":\" ... His novels and poetry have earned international acclaim, and he was the first Canadian ever to win the Man Booker Prize — in 1992, for the wartime story The English Patient. Born in Sri Lanka and educated in England, Ondaatje moved to Canada when he was 18 to attend ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/the-top-20-canadian-books-of-2024-so-far-1.7252475\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d39\"},\"ref\":\"d39\",\"snippet\":\" ... Oz was a writer and journalist whose work has been translated into over forty languages. His last novel, Judas, was shortlisted for the Booker Prize in 2017 and won the Yasnaya Polyana Foreign Fiction Award. He received several international awards, including the Prix Femina, the Israel Prize, the ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/30-books-to-celebrate-30-years-of-writers-company-1.5755144\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"f0f7da6ceb76dfcdf99b0ec3827ec9803e111712d9e4e2a6a9c8ec7aa8c83b32\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"24966c76a85b581a00ef15af8e19df11666e545ad018dcc0517a2ee0ca8cb34e\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"novel translated over 25 languages contender Man Booker International Prize\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_bace400983d04c2ca3defa68"},{"content":"Let me reconsider the puzzle structure carefully. The key constraint is \"the award itself was originally created in the 2000s.\" The Booker Prize (1969) doesn't fit, but the Man Booker International Prize was inaugurated in 2005 (the 2000s).\n\nLet me reconsider: maybe the puzzle is about the regular Booker Prize, and \"originally created in the 2000s\" refers to something else. Or maybe I should look at this differently. Let me reconsider the Obioma lead - \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) was shortlisted for the Booker Prize. In 2019, the Booker was won by \"The Testaments\" (Margaret Atwood) and \"Girl, Woman, Other\" (Bernardine Evaristo). But the Booker Prize was created in 1969, not the 2000s.\n\nLet me reconsider whether the puzzle might involve a different award. Let me check the Man Booker International Prize 2019 winner (Celestial Bodies by Jokha Alharthi) and see if there's a book translated into 25+ languages that was a contender. Let me also reconsider the structure: maybe Book A is a contender for the International Booker Prize, and in the year it was published, another book won the International Booker Prize.\n\nLet me look at the International Booker Prize shortlists and winners in the 2010s more carefully.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"International Booker Prize shortlist 2019 2018 2017 2016 books\", \"Man Booker International Prize 2016 The Vegetarian Han Kang winner shortlist\", \"book translated 30 languages shortlisted International Booker Prize\"]}","name":"search"},"id":"call_f144e13c355e4dc4991a7698","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"The Remainder Alia Trabucco Zeran translated languages\", \"The Shape of the Ruins Juan Gabriel Vasquez translated languages\", \"The Labyrinth of Spirits Juan Gabriel Vasquez International Booker\"]}","name":"search"},"id":"call_19f5f55f5ac84a8e8069aa85","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d15\"},\"ref\":\"d15\",\"snippet\":\" ... Midnight's Children also won a public vote in 2008, on the prize's fortieth anniversary, for \\\"The Best of the Booker\\\". In 2018 a special \\\"Golden Booker\\\" was awarded celebrating 50 years of the award; this was won by Michael Ondaatje for The English Patient.\\n\\nWinners, shortlists ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d14\"},\"ref\":\"d14\",\"snippet\":\" ... of Seven Killings | Historical/experimental novel | |\\n| 2016 | Paul Beatty | The Sellout | Satire | |\\n| 2017 | George Saunders | Lincoln in the Bardo | Historical/experimental novel | |\\n| 2018 | Anna Burns | Milkman | Literary fiction | |\\n| 2019 | Margaret Atwood | The Testaments | Literary fiction | |\\n| 2019 | Bernardine Evaristo The Booker Prizes |url= |access-date=2022-09-26 |website ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d17\"},\"ref\":\"d17\",\"snippet\":\" ... Books by non-white authors have over seven times the likelihood of shortlisting compared to other books (OR: 7.68; p < 0.05). In turn, a book by a non-white author has over 10 times the likelihood of winning the Booker prize compared to other books (OR ... \",\"title\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10837049/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d39\"},\"ref\":\"d39\",\"snippet\":\" ... The last book in the series, The Ghost Road, won the Booker Prize in 1995. Her latest novel, The Silence of the Girls, was shortlisted for the 2019 Women's Prize for Fiction.\\n\\nBarker has been on Writers & Company three times: in 1997, 2015 and 2018.\\n\\n1998: The ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/30-books-to-celebrate-30-years-of-writers-company-1.5755144\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d54\"},\"ref\":\"d54\",\"snippet\":\" ... for Best Novella 2016. My first novel, Sealed (2017), is a work of eco-horror, which was shortlisted for the Not the Booker Award 2018. My second novel, Exit Management (2020), moves between contemporary Britain and 1940s Budapest. It was named a Fiction Book of the Year 2020 ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.durham.ac.uk/staff/naomi-r-booth/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"c2a5fef18d943057b45c10cea0c27271e748b518be814e752d6d2890e0b9742e\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"7984b8eb9c1c0e7152357d45e2042f1bac52cf4341ef2fcd86c6c8247202446c\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"International Booker Prize shortlist 2019 2018 2017 2016 books\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d55\"},\"ref\":\"d55\",\"snippet\":\" ... Her best known novel, The Vegetarian (published in Korea in 2007), was her first to be translated into English, in 2015. It won the Man Booker International Prize in 2016, with the prize split between Han Kang and her translator, Deborah Smith.\\n\\nAt the time, Smith's translation ... \",\"title\":\"https://theconversation.com/my-novels-explore-human-suffering-nobel-prize-winner-han-kang-writes-with-empathy-for-vulnerable-lives-241064\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d56\"},\"ref\":\"d56\",\"snippet\":\" ... literature winner Han Kang was eligible for this year's prize with her book We Do Not Part, translated from Korean by e. yaewon and Paige Aniyah Morris, she did not make the list. Kang won the International Booker in 2016 with her breakthrough novel, The Vegetarian, translated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2025/feb/25/all-13-writers-on-international-booker-longlist-are-first-time-nominees\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d19\"},\"ref\":\"d19\",\"snippet\":\" ... the translator who won the 2016 Man Booker International Prize for her translation of The Vegetarian by Korean author Han Kang\\n\\nIt's of particular importance to note that the winning International Booker Prize comes from an independent press.\\n\\nIn a news conference earlier today, International Booker Prize ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2022/05/geetanjali-shree-and-daisy-rockwell-win-the-international-booker-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d57\"},\"ref\":\"d57\",\"snippet\":\" ... The Accusation, which was written in secret and smuggled out of the country, is his only published book to date. Deborah Smith is the Man Booker International Prize–winning translator of The Vegetarian by Han Kang and other books.\\n\\nHarmless Like You by Rowan Hisayo Buchanan\\n\\nRowan Hisayo ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.aspeninstitute.org/blog-posts/20-new-works-fiction-social-impact/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d58\"},\"ref\":\"d58\",\"snippet\":\" ... And for those of us interested in reading books that originate beyond the English-speaking world, they don't come much more major than the Man Booker International Prize, which was awarded for the first time last year to Han Kang and translator Deborah Smith for The Vegetarian ... \",\"title\":\"https://ayearofreadingtheworld.com/2017/04/29/book-of-the-month-samanta-schweblin/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"569ab9e99ade99a937ee0216f5967d6176919810cfb2ef774b42941a12903aaa\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"0c9aa9d9c9b7f51919011cfe89025be70ed39f68dcd9d1d44b04d0dab478fb9c\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Man Booker International Prize 2016 The Vegetarian Han Kang winner shortlist\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d19\"},\"ref\":\"d19\",\"snippet\":\" ... In a news conference earlier today, International Booker Prize jury chair Frank Wynne credited independent publishers with the lion's share of translated work. \\\"Nobody is surprised that the majority of books on the long- and shortlist,\\\" he said, \\\"are independent publishers. Small independent presses have done enormous ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2022/05/geetanjali-shree-and-daisy-rockwell-win-the-international-booker-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d14\"},\"ref\":\"d14\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 2016, the award was significantly reconfigured, and is now given annually to a single book in English translation, with a £50,000 prize for the winning title, shared equally between author and translator. The award has been known as the International Booker Prize since the Man Group ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d20\"},\"ref\":\"d20\",\"snippet\":\" ... The International Booker Prize 2023 Shortlist\\n\\nAt London Book Fair: Insights Into Translation Buyers\\n\\nAs the news of the International Booker Prize shortlist was announced to the public amid the raucous noise and crush of simultaneously programmed events at London Book Fair's opening today (April 17), the ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2023/04/london-book-fair-the-bookers-new-data-on-translation-buyers/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d21\"},\"ref\":\"d21\",\"snippet\":\" ... His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d59\"},\"ref\":\"d59\",\"snippet\":\" ... of the smallest publisher ever to win the prize, husband-and-wife indie Sort Of Books. In 2022, all the glittering literary prizes went to indies – not only the Booker, but its sister prize for translated fiction, the International Booker, as well as the Nobel, the Goldsmiths, the ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jul/16/uk-indie-publishing-mavericks-shook-up-books-booker-nobel-fitzcarraldo-sort-of-books-daunt\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"f8845b918bcc66aa988b833e3761933c1ded46aeb105179b290e7fdd832f2fc2\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"250ee797d2452e7e5d122a681fa1fcb77d38b269e75d5f002790837b0949f3a0\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"book translated 30 languages shortlisted International Booker Prize\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_f144e13c355e4dc4991a7698"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d60\"},\"ref\":\"d60\",\"snippet\":\" ... So keep reading widely in that language.\\n\\nAbout Sophie Hughes\\n\\nSophie Hughes is a literary translator of Spanish-language writers such as Alia Trabucco Zerán, Laia Jufresa, Rodrigo Hasbún and José Revueltas. She has been shortlisted twice for the International Booker Prize, most recently in 2020 for Fernanda ... \",\"title\":\"https://nationalcentreforwriting.org.uk/writing-hub/five-great-tips-for-getting-started-as-a-literary-translator/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d44\"},\"ref\":\"d44\",\"snippet\":\" ... Amy Arnold's Slip of a Fish landed a 2019 Goldsmiths Prize shortlisting, while Alia Trabucco Zerán's The Remainder was shortlisted for the Man Booker International Prize. Multiple translation prize wins and shortlistings for Gini Alhadeff's translation of I Am the Brother of XX by Fleur ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.andotherstories.org/about-us/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d61\"},\"ref\":\"d61\",\"snippet\":\" ... thriller based in the netherworld of the Anglo-Spanish Costa del Crime, and Alia Trabucco Zerán's LIMPIA (LUMEN), upon which Sophie Hughes is working her magic as we speak. I read only two significant works of poetry this year; Ciaran Carson's brilliant translation from eighteenth-century ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.thewhitereview.org/feature/books-of-the-year-2023/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_r